## What a smart city is

Smart cities are large developments built around the idea of living and working and relaxing in one place. Homes and offices and schools and shops and sports and green spaces share a single master plan. Each one holds a certificate from the Economic Development Board.

## What foreigners can buy

A townhouse or villa or apartment or penthouse or duplex in any approved smart city. A purchase of **USD 375 000 or more** comes with a residence permit.

According to the EDB holders of a residence or occupation or permanent residence permit could also buy a serviced plot of up to 2 100 m² to build on. That was only possible if the purchase was made no later than 30 June 2022.

## The two smart cities on the west coast

The EDB's 2025 summary of smart city projects lists sixteen certificate holders. Two are on our coast:

- **Cap Tamarin** in [Tamarin](/en/areas/tamarin) is planned with residential and commercial and education and leisure zones and a park with a green belt.
- **Medine Smart City** (Uniciti) is listed by the EDB under [Flic en Flac](/en/areas/flic-en-flac). It has an education village with universities and private schools as well as residential estates and a business park and a medical facility and a sports complex and an arts centre.

Ask each developer which phases are for sale and whether a given home qualifies for a residence permit.

## Costs and process

The buying steps are explained in [how buying works](/en/living-in-the-west/how-buying-works). Ask your notary for the registration duty that applies to your purchase.

*Rules and amounts change. Everything here was checked against the Economic Development Board's own pages on 2 October 2026. Confirm the details with the EDB and your notary and the developer before you sign.*
